# {{alternative spelling of|en|ay}}: {{n-g|expressing [[anger]], [[alarm]], [[frustration]], [[pain]], etc.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1799|origyear=1793|author=[[w:August Wilhelm Iffland|W. A. {{quote-gloss|''i.e.'', August Wilhelm}} Iffland]]|chapter_tlr=anonymous|chapter_plain=act III|title=The Bachelors, a Comedy in Five Acts.{{nb...|Translated from the German of W. A. Iffland.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed by}} J{{quote-gloss|ohn}} W{{quote-gloss|alker}} Myers, {{...|Paternostor[sic]-Row,}} for R{{quote-gloss|obert}} Pitkeathley, {{...|Tavistock-Street, Covent Garden;}} and [[w:William West (antiquary)|W{{quote-gloss|illiam}} West]],{{nb...|Paternoster-Row.}}|page=51|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=xbM4AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA51|oclc=3024506|passage=Is it he?—no answer?—it is—it is! Reinhold, Reinhold, the base fiend drives thee by force! '''Aye''', '''aye''', '''aye'''! what nonsense it is!|origtext=de:Iſt’s der? Keine Antwort? — Er iſt’s! Reinhold? Reinhold’, der boͤſe Feind jagt dich parforce! '''Ey''', '''ey''', '''ey'''! Welch Skandal!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1925|month=spring|author=[[w:D. H. Lawrence|D{{quote-gloss|avid}} H{{quote-gloss|erbert}} Lawrence]]|chapter_plain=scene X|title=David: A Play|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Alfred A. Knopf|Alfred A{{quote-gloss|braham}} Knopf]]|year_published=1926|page=69|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015025813414&seq=81|oclc=5243065|passage={{smallcaps|jonathan:}} Oh, peace! Thou art all mischief, Michal, Thou shouldst be married to a Philistine, for his undoing. {{smallcaps|michal:}} '''Ayeee'''! This David has come back to trouble us! Why didst not ''thou'' slay the Philistine, Jonathan?}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=26 January 2020|author=Anthony Colangelo|title=[[w:Roger Federer|{{quote-gloss|Roger}} Federer]] survives another fright to make quarter-finals|work=w:The Age|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200126151517/https://www.theage.com.au/sport/tennis/federer-survives-another-fright-to-make-quarter-finals-20200126-p53uvk.html|location=Melbourne, Vic.|issn=0312-6307|oclc=1058486126|passage="'''Aye''', '''aye''', '''aye'''," Federer said when he hit an uncharacteristically wayward shot when serving for the match, such were his comfort levels.}}
